From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:55:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/22] MoE: the trellis shared expert on a forked stream
 during the router (G6_ROUTE_OVL=1|2, default off)

Trellis-shared layers with separate fc1 / fc2 launches (2+ rows): the shared expert's units read only
x2 (k1.cuh k1_slot: scratch slots n_slots + t, no plan), so they are launched on a side stream forked
before the router GEMV (8 of 48 SMs) and the single-CTA plan kernel, and their weight reads fill the
DRAM time those leave idle. 1 = shared fc1 + fc2 on the fork, joined before the finalize; 2 = shared
fc1 only, joined before the (default) fc2 launch. k1_tr3_fc1_ovl / _fc2_ovl run the shared (PART 1)
or the routed (PART 2) CTAs of k1_tr3_fc1 / _fc2 with the same unit numbering, bodies and scratch:
the same bytes out. In a capture the fork and the join are graph edges. Fused layers (1 row) and the
MTP layer are unchanged. Registers equal the default SH kernels (64, no new spills).
Test: engine/kernels/tests/k1_ovl_test.cu (byte-exact vs default, plain + graph, M 1..12, and a
one-layer bench with the real router GEMV), built by scripts/build.sh.
